        "Transcribed dimensions (mm): base 750; bottom chamfer 25x25; flange edge 110 high, inset 5 over its height; sloping flange top 105 high over 227.5 horizontal; splay 80 high over 50 horizontal to 185 web at y=320; web tapers linearly to 400 at y=850 (TY10).",
        "Shallower members are the same mould truncated at 400+50(n-1) mm (depth ladder printed on the section). Printed web widths at each ladder level (217..400) are rounded values of the linear taper; the implementation uses the exact taper (max difference 0.5 mm).",
        "Property table header prints I as 'x10^10 mm^4'; the values are x10^8 mm^4 (I/yb and I/(D-yb) reproduce the printed Zb/Zt). Stored ixx is printed value x1e8.",
        "Gross concrete section only; strands, links, transverse holes (140 wide slots in elevation), dowel notches and 25x25 end chamfers are not modelled.",
        "Geometry is identical in form to the UK/Irish TY family, but is implemented here from the Ashghal sheet's own dimensions; Ashghal published areas differ from Banagher's (e.g. TY1 188663 vs 188790 mm2)."
